---
import '@/styles/globals.css';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '@/components/Footer.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/Navbar.astro';
import Content from '@/components/Content.astro';
import {Separator} from '@/components/ui/separator';
import Code from '@/components/Code';
import { Card, CardHeader, CardTitle, CardDescription, CardContent, CardFooter } from "@/components/ui/card";
---

<Layout title="Tunnl.app — Get started">
    <Navbar animate={false}/>
    <main class='flex flex-col min-h-screen'>
        <Content>
            <div class='flex flex-col items-center mt-24 p-4'>
                <div class='w-full max-w-xl flex flex-col gap-4 text-lg'>
                    <h1 class='text-5xl font-semibold mb-3'>Quickstart guide</h1>
                    <h2 class='text-3xl font-semibold'>Setup your VPS</h2>
                    <Separator/>
                    <ol class='list-decimal space-y-6 ml-5'>
                        <li>
                            Pick up a cheap VPS with a public IPv4 or IPv6 address, 
                            personally I use a Ubuntu 24.04 Hetzner VPS but you can
                            use any provider.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Setup your user, add your ssh key to the VPS, and allow 
                            port 22/TCP through the firewall.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Install <Code>docker</Code>, <Code>openssl</Code>, 
                            and <Code>jq</Code> on your VPS.
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                    <h2 class='text-3xl font-semibold mt-6'>Install the Tunnl.app dashboard</h2>
                    <Separator/>
                    <ol class='list-decimal space-y-6 ml-5'>
                        <li>
                            <p>
                                Get the quickstart commands by sourcing the install script:
                            </p>
                            <Code className='my-1 p-1'>
                                source &lt;(curl -sL tunnl.app/install.sh)
                            </Code>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Run <Code>tunnl_install</Code> to install the Tunnl.app dashboard,
                            keycloak, Traefik and the Publisher.
                            To uninstall run <Code>tunnl_uninstall</Code> if you
                            want to remove the Tunnl.app quickstart for any reason.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            If you're going to install OpenZiti in a way other than the
                            OpenZiti quickstart answer no to install Ziti. Otherwise
                            answer yes.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            <div class='flex flex-col gap-3'>
                                <p>
                                    Now you need to configure your DNS and get certificates 
                                    for the publisher, the dashboard, and Keycloak services.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    Generally to configure DNS make sure you have these domains
                                    pointing to your VPS.
                                </p>
                                <Code className='p-2'>
                                    <ul class='list-disc ml-5 space-y-1'>
                                        <li>ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; A : VPS IP</li>
                                        <li>publisher.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                        <li>auth.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                        <li>ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                        <li>*.ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN &rarr; CNAME : ziti.ROOT_DOMAIN</li>
                                    </ul>
                                </Code>
                                <p>
                                    To get the IP of your VPS run <Code className='w-fit'>curl -4 ifconfig.io</Code>.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    My preferred way to get certificates is to use the Cloudflare
                                    DNS proxy. The other way is to get certificates through
                                    Traefik with a API key. You could also manage the certificates
                                    externally yourself.
                                </p>
                                <p>
                                    If you're using Cloudflare proxy DNS protect the ROOT_DOMAIN, publisher, and auth
                                    with proxy DNS.
                                </p>
                            </div>
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Create a Keycloak client and configure it for OIDC.
                            Once you do that add those as environemnt variables in
                            <Code>TARGET_DIRECTORY/.keycloak.env</Code>.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Run <Code>docker compose down && docker compose up -d</Code>
                            to redeploy with the new environemnt variables.
                        </li>
                        <li>
                            Test if the dashboard works by going to https://ROOT_DOMAIN,
                            signing in, enrolling an idenity, and creat a service!
                        </li>
                    </ol>
                </div> 
            </div>
        </Content>
        <div class='justify-end pt-10'>
            <Footer />
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
